# The register and ticket board are prose contracts, not source; rewrapping them
# buys nothing and pollutes blame. That is the whole reason: nothing under .icm/ is
# drift-checked. icm-check.sh compares exactly two classes byte-for-byte — .claude/'s
# canonical assets and opencode.jsonc — and everything else in the baseline
# (.icm/CONTEXT.md, .icm/intake/README.md, .claude/settings.json) is seeded when
# missing and never compared again.
.icm/

# Canonical estate assets (hooks, skills) are compared byte-for-byte against
# _system/template/claude/ in icm-board — reformatting them here would trade a
# check failure for silent permanent drift. Agent worktrees under .claude/ also
# carry a full checkout of their own branch, whose formatting is that branch's
# business, not this tree's.
.claude/

# Layer 0 is a prose contract, same reason as .icm/ above — repo-owned, not compared.
AGENTS.md

# The estate rails file is a canonical asset, compared byte-for-byte against
# _system/template/root/ in icm-board. Same trade as above.
opencode.jsonc
